postscript.p:
So poor BoswellThe barrister and literary scholar James Boswell (1778–1822;
                        DNB) had died on 24 February 1822. He had been a fellow pupil with Southey at Westminster School. is
                  dead! – a victim no doubt to the same weakness as his father.James Boswell (1740–1795;
                        DNB), the Scottish biographer and diarist. Both he and his son and namesake were heavy drinkers. There
                  is one good natured man the less in the world, & I have lost in him an old acquaintance who used to meet me with a chearful
                  countenance, & a hearty shake by the hand.
